e":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tickCount"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis: { ticks: { count } }"},{"type":"text","value":" is a hint to the scale. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" for exact tick candidates."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeDot"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add a dot mark wrapped in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused(mark, { match: 'x' })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barGap"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barSize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barY"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barX"},{"type":"text","value":" use pixel "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inset"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxThickness"},{"type":"text","value":"; grouped band padding is a ratio."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseValue"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaY"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y1"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaX"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly. The default baseline is zero."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared tooltip"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focus: 'group-x'"},{"type":"text","value":" and add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":"; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY"},{"type":"text","value":" to focus sparse columns at any x distance."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/marks/bar-and-rect.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bar and Rect"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/marks/line-and-area.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line and Area"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./tooltips-and-focus.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltips and Focus"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./responsive-charts.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive Charts"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for complete examples."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"defaults-to-compare-with-your-existing-charts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defaults to compare with your existing charts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grid lines use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity: 0.11"},{"type":"text","value":", and axis baselines use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.28"},{"type":"text","value":". Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grid"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis.line"},{"type":"text","value":" styles explicitly when matching existing paint. An "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaY"},{"type":"text","value":"\nmark's default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.2"},{"type":"text","value":", set the mark's own opacity when needed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default focus distance is 48 scene pixels. Axis focus modes measure that\ndistance along their axis, so sparse charts can have gaps where nothing takes\nfocus. Keep this default when empty space should clear a tooltip, or choose\nan explicit larger distance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nice: true"},{"type":"text","value":" rounds the domain using the responsive or authored tick count,\neven with a hidden axis. On a small sparkline, use a number such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nice: 5"},{"type":"text","value":"\nto keep the rounding policy independent of its dimensions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rows-without-visible-values","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rows without visible values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus points come from mark geometry. To make a missing-value row available\nto a tooltip, add a zero-radius dot with one point per row and make the\nvisible series "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decorative()"},{"type":"text","value":". The dot's y value must be valid within your\nauthored domain:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"dot(rows, {\n  id: 'row-focus',\n  x: 'gameNumber',\n  y: () => yDomain[0],\n  r: 0,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nearest-x"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group-x"},{"type":"text","value":", this mark supplies the row's semantic x value\nwithout painting a dot. Use the normal keyed rows for keyboard and tooltip\ncontent, and apply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused(..., { match: 'x' })"},{"type":"text","value":" to decorative focus-only\ngeometry. This does not invent a value for the visible series."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"motion-and-tooltips","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion and tooltips"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip motion can inherit chart motion. Give "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip({ motion: ... })"},{"type":"text","value":" its\nown shorter policy or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion: false"},{"type":"text","value":" when a long data transition should not\ncontrol the tooltip. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/motion.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip motion"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"common-options","text":"Common options","level":2},{"id":"defaults-to-compare-with-your-existing-charts","text":"Defaults to compare with your existing charts","level":2},{"id":"rows-without-visible-values","text":"Rows without visible values","level":2},{"id":"motion-and-tooltips","text":"Motion and tooltips","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nUse one `defineChart()` value for marks, scales, guides, and focus. A positional\nscale is an object such as `y: { scale: scaleLinear }`, not `y: scaleLinear`.\nMemoize definitions that capture React props. In Next.js, build them inside\nyour [client component](../framework/react/adapter.md#nextjs-app-router).\n\n## Common options\n\n| Recharts option       | TanStack Charts equivalent                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ResponsiveContainer` | `Chart` observes its container; supply `height` or `aspectRatio`, and `initialWidth` for SSR.                                         |\n| `tickLine={false}`    | `axis: { ticks: { size: 0 } }` keeps labels. `ticks: false` removes both stubs and labels.                                            |\n| `axisLine={false}`    | `axis: { line: false }` hides only the baseline.                                                                                      |\n| `tickCount`           | `axis: { ticks: { count } }` is a hint to the scale. Use `values` for exact tick candidates.                                          |\n| `activeDot`           | Add a dot mark wrapped in `whenFocused(mark, { match: 'x' })`.                                                                        |\n| `barGap` / `barSize`  | `barY` and `barX` use pixel `inset` and `maxThickness`; grouped band padding is a ratio.                                              |\n| `baseValue`           | Set `areaY`'s `y1` or `areaX`'s `x1` explicitly. The default baseline is zero.                                                        |\n| Shared tooltip        | Set `focus: 'group-x'` and add `tooltip`; use `maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY` to focus sparse columns at any x distance. |\n\nSee [Bar and Rect](../reference/marks/bar-and-rect.md),\n[Line and Area](../reference/marks/line-and-area.md),\n[Tooltips and Focus](./tooltips-and-focus.md), and\n[Responsive Charts](./responsive-charts.md) for complete examples.\n\n## Defaults to compare with your existing charts\n\nGrid lines use `strokeOpacity: 0.11`, and axis baselines use `0.28`. Set `grid`\nand `axis.line` styles explicitly when matching existing paint. An `areaY`\nmark's default `fillOpacity` is `0.2`, set the mark's own opacity when needed.\n\nThe default focus distance is 48 scene pixels. Axis focus modes measure that\ndistance along their axis, so sparse charts can have gaps where nothing takes\nfocus. Keep this default when empty space should clear a tooltip, or choose\nan explicit larger distance.\n\n`nice: true` rounds the domain using the responsive or authored tick count,\neven with a hidden axis. On a small sparkline, use a number such as `nice: 5`\nto keep the rounding policy independent of its dimensions.\n\n## Rows without visible values\n\nFocus points come from mark geometry. To make a missing-value row available\nto a tooltip, add a zero-radius dot with one point per row and make the\nvisible series `decorative()`. The dot's y value must be valid within your\nauthored domain:\n\n```ts\ndot(rows, {\n  id: 'row-focus',\n  x: 'gameNumber',\n  y: () => yDomain[0],\n  r: 0,\n})\n```\n\nWith `nearest-x` or `group-x`, this mark supplies the row's semantic x value\nwithout painting a dot. Use the normal keyed rows for keyboard and tooltip\ncontent, and apply `whenFocused(..., { match: 'x' })` to decorative focus-only\ngeometry. This does not invent a value for the visible series.\n\n## Motion and tooltips\n\nTooltip motion can inherit chart motion. Give `tooltip({ motion: ... })` its\nown shorter policy or `motion: false` when a long data transition should not\ncontrol the tooltip. See [Tooltip motion](../reference/motion.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Coming from Recharts\ndescription: Map common Recharts options to chart definitions, marks, scales, focus, and responsive sizing.\n---\n\nUse one `defineChart()` value for marks, scales, guides, and focus. A positional\nscale is an object such as `y: { scale: scaleLinear }`, not `y: scaleLinear`.\nMemoize definitions that capture React props. In Next.js, build them inside\nyour [client component](../framework/react/adapter.md#nextjs-app-router).\n\n## Common options\n\n| Recharts option       | TanStack Charts equivalent                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ResponsiveContainer` | `Chart` observes its container; supply `height` or `aspectRatio`, and `initialWidth` for SSR.                                         |\n| `tickLine={false}`    | `axis: { ticks: { size: 0 } }` keeps labels. `ticks: false` removes both stubs and labels.                                            |\n| `axisLine={false}`    | `axis: { line: false }` hides only the baseline.                                                                                      |\n| `tickCount`           | `axis: { ticks: { count } }` is a hint to the scale. Use `values` for exact tick candidates.                                          |\n| `activeDot`           | Add a dot mark wrapped in `whenFocused(mark, { match: 'x' })`.                                                                        |\n| `barGap` / `barSize`  | `barY` and `barX` use pixel `inset` and `maxThickness`; grouped band padding is a ratio.                                              |\n| `baseValue`           | Set `areaY`'s `y1` or `areaX`'s `x1` explicitly. The default baseline is zero.                                                        |\n| Shared tooltip        | Set `focus: 'group-x'` and add `tooltip`; use `maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY` to focus sparse columns at any x distance. |\n\nSee [Bar and Rect](../reference/marks/bar-and-rect.md),\n[Line and Area](../reference/marks/line-and-area.md),\n[Tooltips and Focus](./tooltips-and-focus.md), and\n[Responsive Charts](./responsive-charts.md) for complete examples.\n\n## Defaults to compare with your existing charts\n\nGrid lines use `strokeOpacity: 0.11`, and axis baselines use `0.28`. Set `grid`\nand `axis.line` styles explicitly when matching existing paint. An `areaY`\nmark's default `fillOpacity` is `0.2`, set the mark's own opacity when needed.\n\nThe default focus distance is 48 scene pixels. Axis focus modes measure that\ndistance along their axis, so sparse charts can have gaps where nothing takes\nfocus. Keep this default when empty space should clear a tooltip, or choose\nan explicit larger distance.\n\n`nice: true` rounds the domain using the responsive or authored tick count,\neven with a hidden axis. On a small sparkline, use a number such as `nice: 5`\nto keep the rounding policy independent of its dimensions.\n\n## Rows without visible values\n\nFocus points come from mark geometry. To make a missing-value row available\nto a tooltip, add a zero-radius dot with one point per row and make the\nvisible series `decorative()`. The dot's y value must be valid within your\nauthored domain:\n\n```ts\ndot(rows, {\n  id: 'row-focus',\n  x: 'gameNumber',\n  y: () => yDomain[0],\n  r: 0,\n})\n```\n\nWith `nearest-x` or `group-x`, this mark supplies the row's semantic x value\nwithout painting a dot. Use the normal keyed rows for keyboard and tooltip\ncontent, and apply `whenFocused(..., { match: 'x' })` to decorative focus-only\ngeometry. This does not invent a value for the visible series.\n\n## Motion and tooltips\n\nTooltip motion can inherit chart motion. Give `tooltip({ motion: ... })` its\nown shorter policy or `motion: false` when a long data transition should not\ncontrol the tooltip. See [Tooltip motion](../reference/motion.md).\n"}
